{
  "title": "Probably delete the repo file-locking scripts",
  "description": "scripts/repo-lock.sh (flock via embedded python3) plus the locking in generate-clients.sh and install-ui-deps.sh guard against concurrent make targets in one worktree corrupting node_modules or generated clients. \
It went through about five rewrites on 2026-10-10 and has about 600 lines of pytest testing bash plumbing (tests/test_repo_lock.py, test_generate_clients_lock.py, test_dependency_lock.py, repo_lock_helpers.py) that run in make test. \
Meanwhile scripts/lint.py runs its own `npm ci` without the lock, and both install paths use `npx -p npm@latest`, so the toolchain isn't actually pinned. \
Owner's expectation: delete it all, since it adds no value. \
First check whether anything actually runs these targets concurrently in one worktree (parallel make? the PostToolUse lint hook racing a manual make?). \
If not, delete repo-lock.sh, its callers' locking, and the lock tests; if so, describe the race to the owner and fix it by making the targets order-safe (for example a stamp file checked against package-lock.json) rather than with a lock. \
Either way, pin the npm version and use one install path.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
